# EVM compatibility

Source of truth: `docs/sprouts/EVM_COMPAT_MATRIX.md` when present (experimental). Hybrid also uses `docs/sprouts/EVM_DEPTH.md`. Do not claim opcode/precompile/fork completeness unless the matrix (or depth doc) row says so.

- Rust owns EVM kernels; Python orchestrates.
- Isolated pytest is **not** EVM acceptance — run the mesh/industrial gate after kernel changes.
- FEATURE/profile: follow ADR 0016; do not mix EVM depth flags into industrial JSON by default.

```text
# ❌ BAD
"EVM is complete / mainnet-equivalent"

# ✅ GOOD
"Opcode X: matrix status <row>. Gaps remain per EVM_COMPAT_MATRIX.md / EVM_DEPTH.md."
```
